      "title": "Echoverse: Deep, evolving environments for computer-use agents",
      "summary": "Scaling fidelity over sheer count, targeting the capabilities agents actually lack, and evolving with the models they train. At a glance We built twelve training worlds for computer-use agents: ten deep domain worlds and two capability worlds, each drilling a single control rendered in many forms (date pickers and nested filters). Depth is what makes them worth training on: these worlds reproduce an application’s real behavior, come seeded with realistic data, and keep state coherent across screens and users. Trained on all twelve, a 9B model nearly doubles its base score (36.5% to 67.1%), coming within fourteen points of GPT-5.4. The experiment taught us several lessons: High simulation fidelity is a must-have; shallow worlds hurt the agent. Trained on shallow and deep builds of the same…",
